      "output": {
        "decision": "answer",
        "reason": "The evidence shows the authors compared Google Translate outputs against U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics data on the percentage of women in each occupation—i.e., U.S. female-worker distribution—and found GT fails to reflect it. However, the evidence does not indicate that they examined the real-world distribution of female workers specifically in the countries where the gender-neutral languages (e.g., Hungarian, Chinese, Yoruba, Basque) are spoken; their demographic comparison uses U.S. BLS data. Thus the evidence fully supports that they examined female-worker distribution via U.S. BLS data and did not report country-specific distributions for the gender-neutral-language countries."
      },
